{
  "version": 1,
  "written": "2026-09-05",
  "purpose": "The upstream each pinned corpus came from, so `npm run drift` (tools/drift.ts) can answer 'has the upstream of this pin moved since it was pinned, and did the pinned bytes move with it?'. Built by hand from every row of fixtures/provenance.md and from the corpus directories walker/scopes.json names; kept by hand. fixtures/provenance.md stays the record of WHAT was pinned and why; this file carries only the liveness relation.",
  "how_to_read": {
    "role": {
      "current": "This pin is what the repository treats as the corpus today. Checked on every run, and its outcome decides the exit code.",
      "historical": "Kept for a finding rather than as the current corpus. Reported as `not_checked`, never counted as current, and never fetched — a superseded pin cannot drift, because nothing claims it is the tip."
    },
    "outcomes": {
      "current": "git: the ref's tip equals pinned_commit. http: the GET body's sha256 equals the pin. ietf-draft: no higher revision exists at the IETF archive.",
      "moved_untouched": "git only: the tip moved but every pinned path is byte-unchanged at the tip. The corpus is still an accurate snapshot of those paths.",
      "moved_changed": "git only: at least one pinned path differs at the tip. Every differing path is listed with its old and new blob id and the new sha256.",
      "changed": "http only: the body's sha256 differs from the pin. Both digests are printed.",
      "superseded": "ietf-draft only: a higher revision exists at the archive; the run names it.",
      "unreachable": "The check could not be made — network, ref or clone failure, with the error text. Never silently a pass.",
      "not_checked": "role: historical. Printed on its own row, never counted as current."
    },
    "blob_ids_not_worktree_bytes": "Every git comparison reads the object store — `git rev-parse HEAD:<path>` for the id, `git cat-file blob <id>` for the bytes — and never a checked-out file. core.autocrlf is true on the machine this repository is developed on, so a worktree comparison would report a change on every text file on every run (fixtures/provenance.md line 398). The tool's clones also set core.autocrlf=false; that is belt and braces, not the mechanism.",
    "pinned_blob_may_be_null": "Where a provenance row gives a blob id, blob ids compare directly. Where it gives only a sha256, the tool digests `git cat-file blob <id>` and compares that. Both read the object store. A row that gives neither cannot be checked and would be a defect in this file.",
    "what_this_file_is_not": "It is not a second copy of fixtures/provenance.md and must not become one. It carries no byte counts, no retrieval narrative and no findings. If a digest here disagrees with fixtures/provenance.md, that file is right and this one is the defect."
  },
  "unmapped": {
    "note": "Provenance rows that map to no upstream entry, listed so the absence is a statement rather than an oversight.",
    "rows": [
      {
        "rows": "the 10 `fixtures/evidence-action/*` rows, source `file://C:/Users/User/agent-action-receipt-vectors/...`",
        "reason": "A local directory, not a network upstream. It is a git repository on this machine (`git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree` returns true, HEAD 4fac3017d2fe19c46b108b012f03abbb77354da1) but `git remote -v` prints nothing, so there is no remote whose tip could be resolved. None of the three kinds fits."
      },
      {
        "rows": "the 81 rows of the 'Generated here, not snapshotted' table",
        "reason": "Produced by tools/make-throwaway-fixtures.mjs, tools/make-acta-fixtures.mjs and by hand. That table's own heading says they are not copies of any published artifact, so they have no upstream by construction."
      },
      {
        "rows": "the 4 `fixtures/insight/execution-receipt-bytes-*.json` package rows",
        "reason": "Email attachments (2026-09-02), copied from cc-output. fixtures/provenance.md records no URL for them and no endpoint served them."
      },
      {
        "rows": "the 2 `fixtures/insight/execution-sample-*.json` rows",
        "reason": "fixtures/provenance.md names the source only as 'production sample endpoint' and records no URL. The pinned registry bytes name https://www.oracleinsight.xyz/api/v1/execution/attestation/sample, but that endpoint mints a fresh signature per call — the two pins 116 minutes apart are both 4675 bytes with different sha256 — so an http entry against it would report `changed` on every run forever. A check that always fails says no more than one that cannot fail."
      },
      {
        "rows": "`fixtures/insight/execution-sample-attestation-2026-09-02T1546Z.json`",
        "reason": "Derived, not fetched: `data.attestation` re-serialised from the row above. test/insight.test.ts asserts it deep-equals its parent, which is a tighter relation than a drift check would be."
      },
      {
        "rows": "every file under `fixtures/delivery/`",
        "reason": "NOT A PROVENANCE ROW AT ALL, and recorded here because that is the finding. walker/scopes.json grades this corpus (21 registered fields, all matching) and fixtures/provenance.md carries no row for any file in it: `grep -c 'fixtures/delivery' fixtures/provenance.md` returns 0. Flagged, not fixed — writing provenance for a corpus is not this file's job."
      },
      {
        "rows": "`cpb/`",
        "reason": "TypeScript sources and Markdown result tables written in this repository. walker/scopes.json registers the directory as a corpus with no rules; there is nothing upstream of it."
      }
    ]
  },
